---
import Layout from '../../components/Layout.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const lang = 'en' as const;
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');

const chapters = (await getCollection('chapters', ({ data }) => data.language === 'en')).sort(
  (a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order
);
const nodes = await getCollection('argument-nodes');
const sources = await getCollection('sources');
---

<Layout
  title="Home"
  lang={lang}
  description="CREDO The Inquiry — A structured inquiry into faith and reason, from foundational questions to theological conclusions."
>
  <h1>CREDO The Inquiry</h1>
  <p
    style="font-family: var(--font-sans); color: var(--color-ink-soft); font-size: var(--fs-small); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; margin: 0 0 var(--gap-2) 0;"
  >
    Faith and reason, structured as argument
  </p>

  <p>
    A structured inquiry: from the problem of evil to the claims of the Church, every step is tested logically
    and grounded in sources. No slogans. No scoring. Only arguments you can verify yourself.
  </p>

  <p>
    The first chapter presents 15 steps of reasoning on divine foreknowledge, human freedom, and the existence
    of evil. The second chapter pursues the question of revelation: if God has reasons we cannot see, would
    God speak? Each step contains a claim, premises, a conclusion, the strongest objection — and its epistemic
    status.
  </p>

  <h2>Start here</h2>
  <ul class="reveal-stagger">
    {
      chapters.map((c) => (
        <li>
          <strong>Chapter {c.data.order}:</strong>{' '}
          <a href={`${base}/en/chapters/${c.data.chapter_slug}`}>{c.data.title}</a>
          <div style="font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: var(--fs-small); color: var(--color-ink-faint);">
            {c.data.nodes_used.length} steps · {c.data.sources_used.length} sources
          </div>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>

  <h2>Site structure</h2>
  <ul class="reveal-stagger">
    <li>
      <a href={`${base}/en/nodes`}>{nodes.length} argument steps</a> (POE-001 through POE-015; REV-001 through REV-009)
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href={`${base}/en/sources`}>{sources.length} sources</a> — Scripture, theology, church documents, scholarship
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Reasoning principles</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>No invented quotations, sources, page numbers, or Catholic doctrine.</li>
    <li>Textual claims are kept separate from theological claims.</li>
    <li>Conclusions are bounded by premises.</li>
    <li>
      Foreknowledge, causation, permission, intention, possibility, plausibility, defense, and theodicy remain
      distinct.
    </li>
    <li>Plantinga's Free Will Defense is presented as a defense, not as a complete solution.</li>
    <li>Fallen angels are not invoked to explain particular natural disasters.</li>
    <li>Not every natural evil is mapped to a particular sin.</li>
    <li>Catholicism is not declared established before the relevant arguments are developed.</li>
    <li>No arbitrary numerical scores for worldviews.</li>
  </ol>
</Layout>
